# Hub-side alarm for satellite claims that go quiet (local-satellite-stale,
# sd:2918). A satellite session claims an item with `sd-db.sh claim`; this
# job fetches each claimed branch and sends one alert per stale episode
# through local-notify when no note, item update or pushed commit landed for
# SD_SATELLITE_STALE_HOURS (default 3).
#
# Hub only: install it in `<config>/cron-jobs/jobs/<hub host>/`. On a
# satellite the verb refuses with HubOnly.
#
# Every 30 minutes, all day: cron-jobs.sh takes no hour ranges, so the verb
# holds the alert window itself (SD_SATELLITE_STALE_WINDOW, default 7-22
# local hours) and sends nothing outside it.
#
# It exits 1 only when an alert was not delivered, so the failure push covers
# a lost alert. The nightly health check runs `status` through its sweep as
# the backstop; the cron watchdog flags this job if launchd stops firing it.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/30 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="10m"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-satellite-stale/satellite-stale.sh\" run"
